---
import { Bell } from '@lucide/astro'
---

<section class="notice-band on-night" aria-labelledby="notice-title">
  <div class="wrap notice-band-grid">
    <div class="notice-band-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--night"><span class="dot"></span> Reminders</span>
      <h2 id="notice-title">The one alert that reaches you <em>mid-flow.</em></h2>
      <p>
        Notifications usually land in a corner you are not looking at. Notch puts the card directly
        under the collapsed tab, at the top of the screen, for twelve seconds — over whatever has
        focus.
      </p>

      <ul class="notice-points">
        <li><Bell size={13} /> Title and time, no window to close.</li>
        <li>It never steals focus from your editor.</li>
        <li>The system notification still lands where Windows allows it.</li>
      </ul>

      <a class="link link--night" href="/help#reminder-missing">How reminders work</a>
    </div>

    <figure class="notice-figure">
      <img
        src="/screenshots/notice.png"
        width="1588"
        height="404"
        alt="The collapsed notch bar with a reminder card below it: “Reminder · Stand up and stretch, Today at 3:30 PM”."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Real screenshot · collapsed bar and reminder card</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
